</p>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#666;text-align:center">Member portal: https://www.meridianhealth.example/members/prior-auth (status check, same account)</p>

<p>The member channel collects: your <b>member ID + date of birth + last four of SSN</b>, the
<b>March MRI report and images</b> (CD/DICOM upload), and the surgical notes from your
April consult. Verification completes same-day; the auth holds.</p>

<h3>3. What Voiding Means</h3>
<ul>
<li>May 26 proceeds as self-pay: estimated <b>$14,200</b> (facility + surgeon + anesthesia)</li>
<li>Or the slot cancels: Crest Surgical Center's next opening is late July (Dr. Feldman books out)</li>
<li>A new authorization starts from zero (peer-to-peer review, 7-10 business days)</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF3E0;padding:12px">An insurer email asking for SSN digits and
medical images deserves your hardest look — health phishing is rampant, and your caution protects
both your coverage and your records. Checks: the authorization number above matches your approval
letter; the status "re-review" is visible on the member portal (address above); and the safest
alternative is to call the utilization-management number on the back of your card and let
<b>Dr. Feldman's office run the clinic re-submission on an expedited basis</b> — but the 72-hour
window is set by the re-review clock, not by our convenience.</p>

